      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing the unused `ALL` field\n2. Renaming the opaque `_set()` helper to `propertySet()`\n3. Using descriptive variable names instead of `v1`/`v2`\n4. Adding a brief comment explaining the test's intentThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes the unused `ALL` field, renames `_set()` to `propertySet()` for clarity, uses descriptive variable names `valueWithAB`/`valueWithCD` instead of `v1`/`v2`, and adds a concise comment explaining the test's intent — all without changing the runtime behavior."
